---
description: Baseline house style for readable, maintainable changes
alwaysApply: true
---

house-style:

- Small, focused changes with one clear purpose per commit.
- Descriptive names. No single-letter variables outside tight loops.
- Comments only where the logic is non-obvious.
- Match the surrounding file's idiom rather than introducing a new one.
- Update user-facing docs in the same change as the behaviour.
